        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Wool sampler by Mary Ann Body, embroidered with silk; English, 1789."@en , "The earliest samplers were reference works for embroiderers. They showed 'samples' of patterns and stitches and recorded how to achieve particular effects. In Europe in the 17th century samplers provided instruction and practice for girls learning needlework. Embroiderers began to make more use of picture decoration. By about 1750, the house and garden had become, and remained, a favourite choice of subject. Here the needleworker has combined it with a moral verse, as well as her name and age and the date it was completed."@en , "Embroidered sampler"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/bf97b748-544e-348e-8058-0b0a0e06e1ce> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f4aed58e-95bb-320d-a982-dd3a606b29c5> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/d1284bd8-235d-3713-be92-3bfef040daca> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/34037c82-8fb4-3146-996f-67afb5ef4d45> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/744c83ce-ec9b-35ca-a370-185280072d91> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Embroidered sampler"@en , "The earliest samplers were reference works for embroiderers. They showed 'samples' of patterns and stitches and recorded how to achieve particular effects. In Europe in the 17th century samplers provided instruction and practice for girls learning needlework. Embroiderers began to make more use of picture decoration. By about 1750, the house and garden had become, and remained, a favourite choice of subject. Here the needleworker has combined it with a moral verse, as well as her name and age and the date it was completed."@en , "Wool sampler by Mary Ann Body, embroidered with silk; English, 1789."@en ;
